POSIX strerror_r() returns int while the GNU variant returns char*.
Building against musl (or any POSIX libc) with a compiler that promotes
-Wint-conversion to an error (zig cc / clang 20, gcc 14) fails with:
  error: incompatible integer to pointer conversion assigning to 'char *' from 'int'
Only the filled buffer is used, so the return value is simply discarded.

--- a/mosquitto.c
+++ b/mosquitto.c
@@ -888,8 +888,10 @@
 
 PHP_MOSQUITTO_API char *php_mosquitto_strerror_wrapper(int err)
 {
-	char *ret, *buf = ecalloc(256, sizeof(char));
-	ret = strerror_r(err, buf, 256);
+	char *buf = ecalloc(256, sizeof(char));
+	/* strerror_r() returns char* on GNU libc but int on POSIX (musl, macOS).
+	 * Only the filled buffer is used, so the return value is discarded. */
+	(void) strerror_r(err, buf, 256);
 	if (!buf[0]) {
 		efree(buf);
 		return NULL;
